{
  "uid": "bct-analytics-pipeline",
  "title": "BCT - Analytics pipeline",
  "description": "CDC pipeline and warehouse health for project odoo19-bct.\n\nOwned by the Data Warehouse agent (contract 04 section 7: observability/grafana/dashboards/analytics-*.json).\n\nEvery panel reads the prometheus datasource. Nothing here queries the warehouse directly: a Grafana datasource is reachable by every user with Editor rights, and business data belongs behind RLS with a tenant scope, which a shared dashboard connection does not have. Row counts, timestamps and test outcomes are operational, and that is all this dashboard shows.",
  "tags": [
    "analytics",
    "warehouse",
    "cdc",
    "odoo19-bct"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "editable": true,
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "refresh": "30s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-6h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "tenant",
        "label": "Tenant",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "prometheus"
        },
        "query": {
          "query": "label_values(bct_warehouse_pipeline_rows_loaded, tenant)",
          "refId": "tenant"
        },
        "refresh": 2,
        "includeAll": true,
        "multi": true,
        "current": {},
        "options": [],
        "description": "Tenant slug. dim_tenant flags is_test_tenant, so a test tenant volume is never mistaken for real volume."
      }
    ]
  },
  "annotations": {
    "list": [
      {
        "builtIn": 1,
        "datasource": {
          "type": "grafana",
          "uid": "-- Grafana --"
        },
        "enable": true,
        "hide": true,
        "iconColor": "rgba(0, 211, 255, 1)",
        "name": "Annotations & Alerts",
        "type": "dashboard"
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Replication slot lag - the 2 GB safety valve",
      "id": 1,
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "WAL retained per replication slot (from Postgres itself)",
      "id": 2,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 16,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "pg_replication_slots_pg_wal_lsn_diff{slot_name=~\"bct_slot_.*\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{slot_name}}",
          "range": true,
          "instant": false,
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "536870912",
          "legendFormat": "warn - 512 MiB (platform.rules)",
          "range": true,
          "instant": false,
          "refId": "B"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "1073741824",
          "legendFormat": "critical - 1 GiB (platform.rules)",
          "range": true,
          "instant": false,
          "refId": "C"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "2147483648",
          "legendFormat": "cap - max_slot_wal_keep_size 2 GiB",
          "range": true,
          "instant": false,
          "refId": "D"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "unit": "bytes",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 536870912
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 1073741824
              }
            ]
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": true
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ],
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "description": "THE PRIMARY SIGNAL, and it comes from postgres_exporter rather than from the CDC consumer. The failure the 2 GB cap exists to bound is the consumer being dead - at which point bct_cdc_replication_slot_lag_bytes goes ABSENT, not high, and an alert on it never fires. This series is emitted by Postgres itself and survives the death of the consumer.\n\nCrossing the cap does not damage Odoo - that is the entire point of the cap - but Postgres invalidates the slot and the warehouse then needs a full resync."
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Consumer vs Postgres disagreement",
      "id": 3,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 1
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "max by (tenant) (pg_replication_slots_pg_wal_lsn_diff{slot_name=~\"bct_slot_.*\"}) - on(tenant) group_right() max by (tenant) (bct_cdc_replication_slot_lag_bytes)",
          "legendFormat": "{{tenant}}",
          "range": false,
          "instant": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "unit": "bytes",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 268435456
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      },
      "description": "Neither number alone catches a consumer that BELIEVES it is caught up: it reports low lag while Postgres reports high lag, because confirmed_flush_lsn is not advancing. Their difference does. Alerts above 256 MiB."
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Slot invalidated",
      "id": 4,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 6
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "max(bct_cdc_slot_invalidated) or on() vector(0)",
          "legendFormat": "invalidated",
          "range": false,
          "instant": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "mappings": [],
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "orange",
                "value": 1
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 2
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      },
      "description": "1 means the cap fired and the warehouse has a hole in it. A resync from snapshot is required; the consumer must not silently reconnect."
    },
